Problem statement: 
Roman numerals are formed by appending the conversions of decimal place values from highest to lowest. Converting a decimal place value into a Roman numeral has the following rules:

We use Java
For this we use HashMaps. We manage 4 Strings[] for M, D, C, X
Each C, X, I; consists of 10 symbols having value 100-900 & 10-90 & 1-9. (In Roamn value)

As we traverse from left to right, we use a numerical formula: 
M[num/1000] + C[(num%1000)/100] + X[(num%100)/10] +[(num%10)]
